messages.body_plain:
S-Plus Group:

I'm trying to set values for a number of variables (>10) to missing based on
a specified condition (i.e. var > some value).

In the past I've done this in SAS, but would like to learn how to do this in
S-Plus.

For example my SAS code would be something like...

data libname.data2;
   set libname.data1;
array temp{10} var1-var10;
do i = 1 to 10;
   if temp{i} > 5 then temp{i} = .;
end;
run;

This sets to missing any values >5 for each of the 10 variables.  Note that
my variables are not necessarily named sequentially so I would have to list
them rather than use a range.

Can I do something similar in S-Plus?

Thank you.

Marc

